For encrypting data during export, you can use a combination of data-in-transit encryption, such as Transport Layer Security (TLS), to secure the communication channel, and object encryption to encrypt individual objects for the recipient. Data-in-transit encryption ensures that the data is protected while being transmitted over the network. Object encryption, on the other hand, provides an extra layer of security by encrypting the data at the source before transmission, ensuring that it remains secure until it is decrypted by the intended recipient. This is especially important in high-risk scenarios where the data may be intercepted during transmission.

